<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2013a" Name="PPAR signaling pathway" Data-Source="WikiPathways" Version="WP5642_r20260819173100" Author="[MadhushriMSV, Egonw]" Last-Modified="20260819173100" Organism="Gadus morhua">
  <Comment Source="WikiPathways-description">PPAR signaling pathway in Gadus morhua. This pathway was inferred from Danio rario pathway [WP4020](https://www.wikipathways.org/instance/WP4020). Proteins on this pathway were identified in Gadus morhua using data from FairdomHub repository: [10.15490/fairdomhub.1.study.753.2](https://doi.org/10.15490/fairdomhub.1.study.753.2).Peroxisome proliferator-activated receptors (PPARs) are nuclear hormone receptors that are activated by fatty acids and their derivatives. PPAR has three subtypes (PPARalpha, beta/delta, and gamma) showing different expression patterns in vertebrates. Each of them is encoded in a separate gene and binds fatty acids and eicosanoids. PPARalpha plays a role in the clearance of circulating or cellular lipids via the regulation of gene expression involved in lipid metabolism in liver and skeletal muscle. PPARbeta/delta is involved in lipid oxidation and cell proliferation. PPARgamma promotes adipocyte differentiation to enhance blood glucose uptake. Source [KEGG](http://www.genome.jp/dbget-bin/www_bget?pathway+dre03320).</Comment>
  <Comment Source="ECO">ECO:0007481 - biological system reconstruction evidence based on orthology evidence used in automatic assertion</Comment>
  <Comment Source="HomologyMapper">This pathway was inferred from Danio rerio pathway Dr_PPAR_signaling_pathway_WP4020_20210515.gpml.gpml (WP4020_r123454) with a 77.0% conversion rate.</Comment>
